      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Higher doses carry a greater risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia, and they haven't been shown to work better. Normal renal and hepatic function doesn't change that ceiling.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n1. **A typo or unit slip.** Sertraline is usually started at 25\u201350 mg daily and titrated to a usual range of 50\u2013200 mg daily. I can enter 200 mg PO daily or another dose you choose.\n2. **A deliberate supratherapeutic dose.** If so, please confirm and add a brief rationale. I can put it in the order note, for example \"Dose exceeds labeled max, confirmed by attending.\" Pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n3. **A different drug or indication.** I can change the order if you meant something else.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
